                                                    </a>
                                                    <em>(Blog post, 2018-05-03)</em>
                                                </p>
                                                <p>
                                                    <a href="https://iiif.io/api/image/3.0/">
                                                        IIIF Image API Documentation
                                                    </a>
                                                    <em>(Documentation)</em>
                                                </p>
                                            </td>
                                        </tr>
                                    </table>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li class="item">
                            <figure>
                                <div class="iconic-container">
                                    <a href="https://id.loc.gov/">
                                        <img
                                            class="iconic"
                                            src="https://labs.loc.gov/static/labs/data/images/apis/lds.png"
                                            alt="Red text that reads ID.LOC.GOV with an image of the interior of the Library of Congress Jefferson building."
                                        />
                                    </a>
                                </div>
                            </figure>
                            <div class="description">
                                <div class="item-description">
                                    <span class="item-description-title">
                                        <a href="https://id.loc.gov/">Linked Data Service</a>
                                    </span>
                                    <span class="item-description-abstract">
                                        The Linked Data Service provides interactive and machine
                                        access to the Library's authority and bibliographic
                                        metadata, along with commonly-found standards and
                                        vocabularies used and/or maintained by the Library of
                                        Congress.
                                    </span>
                                    <table class="table-bordered table-padded table-full-width">
                                        <tr>
                                            <th scope="row">Official documentation</th>
                                            <td>
                                                <a href="https://id.loc.gov/">
                                                    https://id.loc.gov/
                                                </a>
                                            </td>
                                        </tr>

                                        <tr>
                                            <th scope="row">Resources</th>
                                            <td>
                                                <p>
                                                    <a href="https://id.loc.gov/techcenter/">
                                                        Linked Data Service Technical Center
                                                    </a>
                                                </p>
                                                <p>
                                                    <a
                                                        href="https://blogs.loc.gov/thesignal/2019/05/integrating-wikidata-at-the-library-of-congress/"
                                                    >
                                                        Integrating Wikidata at the Library of
                                                        Congress
                                                    </a>
                                                    <em>(Blog post, 2019-05-22)</em>
                                                </p>
                                            </td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <th scope="row">Notes</th>
                                            <td>
                                                Each controlled vocabulary list has a resolvable
                                                URI, as does each data value within it. Ontologies
                                                for several major data element sets are also
                                                available. URIs accessible at id.loc.gov link to
                                                bibliographic descriptions and controlled
                                                vocabularies and the values within them. This data
                                                service does not provide access to the physical or
                                                electronic holdings of the Library.
                                            </td>
                                        </tr>
                                    </table>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li class="item">
                            <figure>
                                <div class="iconic-container">
                                    <a href="https://api.nlsbard.loc.gov/">
                                        <img
                                            class="iconic"
                                            src="https://labs.loc.gov/static/labs/data/images/apis/nls.png"
                                            alt="The black and organge logo for the National Library Service for the Blind and Print Disabled"
                                        />
                                    </a>
                                </div>
                            </figure>
                            <div class="description">
                                <div class="item-description">
                                    <span class="item-description-title">
                                        <a href="https://api.nlsbard.loc.gov/">
                                            National Library Service (NLS) Bard API
                                        </a>
                                    </span>
                                    <span class="item-description-abstract">
                                        The Bard Public API allows searches to be performed against
                                        the metadata for the entire BARD collection of the National
                                        Library Service for the Blind and Print Disabled.
                                    </span>
                                    <table class="table-bordered table-padded table-full-width">
                                        <tr>
                                            <th scope="row">Official documentation</th>
                                            <td>
                                                <a href="https://api.nlsbard.loc.gov/">
                                                    https://api.nlsbard.loc.gov/
                                                </a>
                                            </td>
                                        </tr>

                                        <tr>
                                            <th scope="row">Notes</th>
                                            <td>
                                                It does not currently allow searches to be performed
                                                against the text inside an item. Use of the API does
                                                not require password authentication.
                                            </td>
                                        </tr>
                                    </table>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li class="item">
                            <figure>
                                <div class="iconic-container">
                                    <a href="https://www.loc.gov/pictures/api">
                                        <img class="iconic" src="" alt="" />
                                    </a>
                                </div>
                            </figure>
                            <div class="description">
                                <div class="item-description">
                                    <span class="item-description-title">
                                        <a href="https://www.loc.gov/pictures/api">
                                            Prints and Photographs Online Catalog (PPOC) JSON API
                                        </a>
                                    </span>
                                    <span class="item-description-abstract">
                                        The PPOC API enables access to the content in the Library of
                                        Congress's Prints and Photographs Online Catalog, a website
                                        focused on the Library's collection of still pictures,
                                        including photographs, fine and popular prints and drawings,
                                        posters, and architectural and engineering drawings.
                                    </span>
                                    <table class="table-bordered table-padded table-full-width">
                                        <tr>
                                            <th scope="row">Official documentation</th>
                                            <td>
                                                <a href="https://www.loc.gov/pictures/api">
                                                    https://www.loc.gov/pictures/api
                                                </a>
                                            </td>
                                        </tr>

                                        <tr>
                                            <th scope="row">Notes</th>
                                            <td>
                                                Most of the content in PPOC is also accessible via
                                                the loc.gov APIs.
                                            </td>
                                        </tr>
                                    </table>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li class="item">
                            <figure>
                                <div class="iconic-container">
                                    <a
                                        href="https://www.loc.gov/standards/sru/resources/lcServers.html"
                                    >
                                        <img class="iconic" src="" alt="" />
                                    </a>
                                </div>
                            </figure>
                            <div class="description">
                                <div class="item-description">
                                    <span class="item-description-title">
                                        <a
                                            href="https://www.loc.gov/standards/sru/resources/lcServers.html"
                                        >
                                            Search/Retrieval via URL
                                        </a>
                                    </span>
                                    <span class="item-description-abstract">
                                        The Search/Retrieval via URL (SRU) servers provide access to
                                        Library data, including the catalog and some authority
                                        files, via SRU, a standard XML-based protocol for search
                                        queries which utilizes the Contextual Query Language (CQL),
                                        a standard syntax for representing queries.
                                    </span>
                                    <table class="table-bordered table-padded table-full-width">
                                        <tr>
                                            <th scope="row">Official documentation</th>
                                            <td>
                                                <a
                                                    href="https://www.loc.gov/standards/sru/resources/lcServers.html"
                                                >
                                                    https://www.loc.gov/standards/sru/resources/lcServers.html
                                                </a>
                                            </td>
                                        </tr>

                                        <tr>
                                            <th scope="row">Resources</th>
                                            <td>
                                                <p>
                                                    <a
                                                        href="https://www.loc.gov/standards/sru/misc/simple.html"
                                                    >
                                                        SRU is Simple!
                                                    </a>
                                                    <em>(Guide)</em>
                                                </p>
                                            </td>
                                        </tr>
                                    </table>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li class="item">
                            <figure>
                                <div class="iconic-container">
                                    <a
                                        href="https://www.loc.gov/apis/micro-services/streaming-services/"
                                    >
                                        <img class="iconic" src="" alt="" />
                                    </a>
                                </div>
                            </figure>
                            <div class="description">
                                <div class="item-description">
                                    <span class="item-description-title">
                                        <a
                                            href="https://www.loc.gov/apis/micro-services/streaming-services/"
                                        >
                                            Streaming Services API
                                        </a>
                                    </span>
                                    <span class="item-description-abstract">
                                        Streaming Services is an audio and video (A/V) delivery API
                                        based largely on the IIIF Image 2 API which image services
                                        implements. In a similar manner, A/V files are accessible by
                                        a URI that specifies the region, size, rotation, temporal
                                        region, quality characteristics and format of the requested
                                        file.
                                    </span>
                                    <table class="table-bordered table-padded table-full-width">
                                        <tr>
                                            <th scope="row">Official documentation</th>
                                            <td>
                                                <a
                                                    href="https://www.loc.gov/apis/micro-services/streaming-services/"
                                                >
                                                    https://www.loc.gov/apis/micro-services/streaming-services/
                                                </a>
                                            </td>
                                        </tr>

                                        <tr>
                                            <th scope="row">Resources</th>
                                            <td>
                                                <p>
                                                    <a href="https://iiif.io/api/image/2.0/">
                                                        IIIF Image API 2.0 Documentation
                                                    </a>
                                                    <em>(Documentation)</em>
                                                </p>
                                            </td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <th scope="row">Notes</th>
                                            <td>
                                                A URI can also be constructed to request basic
                                                technical information about the resource to support
                                                client applications. This API was conceived of to
                                                facilitate systematic reuse of AV resources in
                                                digital AV repositories maintained by cultural
                                                heritage organizations. It could be adopted by any
                                                AV repository or service, and can be used to
                                                retrieve static AV in response to a properly
                                                constructed URI.
                                            </td>
                                        </tr>
                                    </table>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li class="item">
                            <figure>
                                <div class="iconic-container">
                                    <a
                                        href="https://www.loc.gov/apis/micro-services/text-services/"
                                    >
                                        <img class="iconic" src="" alt="" />
                                    </a>
                                </div>
                            </figure>
                            <div class="description">
                                <div class="item-description">
                                    <span class="item-description-title">
                                        <a
                                            href="https://www.loc.gov/apis/micro-services/text-services/"
                                        >
                                            Text Services API
                                        </a>
                                    </span>
                                    <span class="item-description-abstract">
                                        The text-services API provides access to the full text, word
                                        coordinates and context snippets for certain image based
                                        sets of content on loc.gov. These content sets include but
                                        not limited to newspapers and selected digitized books.
                                    </span>
                                    <table class="table-bordered table-padded table-full-width">
                                        <tr>
                                            <th scope="row">Official documentation</th>
